profile.FAST=Fast
profile.REFERENCE=Reference
profile.HIGH=High
screen.LIGHTING=Light and colour
screen.CLOUDS=Overcast sky
screen.FOG=Layered valley mist
screen.WATER=Water
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.0=Sky only
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.1=Reference (24 steps)
value.REFLECTION_QUALITY.2=High (48 steps)
option.AMBIENT_BRIGHTNESS=Ambient brightness
option.AMBIENT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Scales sky-lit surfaces while retaining Minecraft lightmap levels.
option.ambientOcclusionLevel=Ambient occlusion
option.ambientOcclusionLevel.comment=Independent amount of vanilla corner/contact shading; lower keeps foliage open.
option.COLOUR_TEMPERATURE=Colour temperature
option.COLOUR_TEMPERATURE.comment=Small fixed balance adjustment. Zero keeps neutral foreground colours.
option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.SATURATION.comment=Subtle global colour saturation; all presets use the same value.
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE=Cloud coverage
option.CLOUD_COVERAGE.comment=One produces an unbroken grey ceiling. Lower values soften toward blue-grey sky.
option.CLOUD_SCALE=Cloud band scale
option.CLOUD_SCALE.comment=World size of broad cloud forms, in approximate blocks.
option.CLOUD_IRREGULARITY=Cloud irregularity
option.CLOUD_IRREGULARITY.comment=Broad domain warping breaks up the elongated cloud layers.
option.CLOUD_SHADING=Cloud shading
option.CLOUD_SHADING.comment=Contrast within the overcast ceiling; no sharp puffy clouds.
option.CLOUD_SPEED=Cloud movement
option.CLOUD_SPEED.comment=Slow world-anchored drift. Zero freezes movement.
option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud samples
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=Additional low-frequency detail; does not alter the colour palette.
option.FOG_DENSITY=Valley mist density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Outdoor mist amount. Fluid and status fog remain controlled by Minecraft.
option.FOG_HEIGHT=Mist layer altitude
option.FOG_HEIGHT.comment=World Y of the lower mist layer; move this for high-altitude terrain.
option.FOG_FALLOFF=Mist height falloff
option.FOG_FALLOFF.comment=How slowly the mist density decreases above the valley.
option.FOG_START=Clear foreground distance
option.FOG_START.comment=Mist starts gradually beyond this distance, in blocks.
option.FOG_QUALITY=Mist samples
option.FOG_QUALITY.comment=Spatial integration accuracy, with the same density and layer settings.
option.WATER_REFLECTION=Water reflection strength
option.WATER_REFLECTION.comment=Reflection and sky sheen on water top faces only. Solids stay matte.
option.REFLECTION_QUALITY=Terrain reflection quality
option.REFLECTION_QUALITY.comment=Fast uses sky only; Reference traces 24 steps; High traces 48 steps.
option.REFLECTION_DISTANCE=Reflection ray distance
option.REFLECTION_DISTANCE.comment=Maximum terrain ray length. Missing scenery fades to the procedural sky.
option.WATER_TRANSPARENCY=Shallow water clarity
option.WATER_TRANSPARENCY.comment=Controls visibility at the shore; deeper water still absorbs colour.
option.WATER_ABSORPTION=Water absorption
option.WATER_ABSORPTION.comment=Depth-dependent loss of visibility, strongest in the red channel.
option.RIPPLE_STRENGTH=Ripple strength
option.RIPPLE_STRENGTH.comment=Small water normal changes; shorelines and block geometry stay fixed.
option.RIPPLE_SCALE=Ripple frequency
option.RIPPLE_SCALE.comment=Spatial frequency of the three unequal ripple layers.
option.RIPPLE_SPEED=Ripple speed
option.RIPPLE_SPEED.comment=Surface movement speed. Zero freezes water shading.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS=Block-light brightness
option.BLOCKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Lightmap block light and emissive interiors; no large bloom halo.
option.BLOCKLIGHT_WARMTH=Block-light warmth
option.BLOCKLIGHT_WARMTH.comment=Amber light temperature, strongest away from daylight.
